{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm thinking about starting a small community radio station to broadcast local news and music in my area of Kenya. Based on what I need to know about getting a broadcasting license, what steps do I need to follow and what should I be watching for?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "To start a community radio station in Kenya, you'll need to watch for official announcements. The Communications Authority publishes available radio frequencies and channels in Kenyan newspapers and on their website. That publication is your signal to start the application process. Once you see those announcements, you'll have a specific timeframe to submit your license application for the broadcasting service you want to provide. So your first step is to regularly check newspapers and the CA website for these frequency listings, because that's when the application window opens. Make sure you apply within the deadline they give, or you'll have to wait for the next round of frequencies to become available."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "ca_licensing_procedures.txt", "source_text": "list of available frequencies / channels in at least one print media in Kenya and on the CA website informing interested applicants to apply for provision of the identified broadcasting service (s). Such publication shall be the trigger point for interested applicants to submit application for specific licenses within the time frame specified. Download: Framework on the Application and Usage of DVB Identifiers in Kenya Download: Minimum Technical Requirements for DVB-T2 Receivers in Kenya Proced"}}
