{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm a small business owner in Kenya and I've heard about withholding tax changes from 2019. Can you explain in simple terms what the government did with withholding tax and why?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "In October 2019, the Kenyan government expanded withholding tax to cover more types of services beyond just management and professional fees. The main reason was to widen the tax base—meaning they wanted to collect taxes from a broader range of business services. If your business pays for services, you may now need to withhold tax on some of these payments, not just the management and professional fees like before. You should check which specific services are now included to make sure you're withholding correctly."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "summarization", "source_filename": "doing_business_kenya_sme_guide_2024.pdf", "source_text": "ated by the restructuring of corporate entities in order to allow efficiency and market penetration in corporate entities. Effective Date 1st October 2019 WITHHOLDING TAX Expansion of Withholding Tax Base In order to widen the tax base, The Cabinet Secretary for the National Treasury through Finance Bill 2019 proposed to expand the scope of application of withholding tax by subjecting additional services, other than management and professional fees to withholding taxes. These services include: s"}}
