{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm running a small farm supply business and I've heard about cooperatives having problems with loans. What does the source text say are the main issues cooperatives faced with loan repayment?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "According to the source, cooperatives faced serious problems when many farmers defaulted on their loan repayments. This left the cooperative societies holding large amounts of unpaid loans from financial institutions. The situation got so bad that some farmers even stopped farming altogether. The government eventually had to write off these loans to try to get farmers back into production. The key lesson here is that when farmers can't repay loans, it creates a chain reaction that hurts the whole cooperative system."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "summarization", "source_filename": "un_msme_formalization_guidelines_kenya.pdf", "source_text": "up at their gates. This led to the defaulting by many farmers on their loan repayment obligations, with the societies left with huge unserviced loans from financial institutions. Other farmers simply abandoned their farming activities. Indeed, the government was forced to write off the loans to bring farmers back to production. Another illustration of how different sector policies and programmes have impacted the performance of cooperatives involves the Kilimo Biashara (farming as a business) pr"}}
