{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I run a small digital payment service that helps customers in my area send money to family in other counties. We're based in Nairobi and have 3 staff members. Do I need any special telecommunications license from the regulator, and what category would my business fall under?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Based on the information available, your digital payment service would likely be classified as an Application Service Provider (ASP) if you're offering services over telecommunications networks. The regulator does track ASPs as a licensed category — in fact, the number of ASPs grew significantly from 330 in FY 2019/20 to 441 by FY 2021/22. However, the source text doesn't provide the specific requirements for ASP licensing or the application process. You should contact the Communications Authority of Kenya directly to confirm whether your payment service needs ASP licensing, what the application steps are, and any fees involved. Don't assume you're exempt just because you're small — licensing requirements apply based on the type of service, not the business size."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "ca_annual_report_2023_2024.pdf", "source_text": "communicate, share information and transact. This section highlights achievements in telecommunications licensing, scarce frequency spectrum and numbering assignments, type-approval/acceptance/clearance of equipment, management of the cybersecurity infrastructure as well as Universal Service Fund (USF) initiatives. Table 1.8 Number of Telecommunications Licensees by Category LICENCE CATEGORY FY 2019/20 FY 2020/21 FY 2021/22 FY 2022/23 FY 2023/24 Application Service Providers (ASP) 330 388 441 50"}}
