{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I run a small retail shop in Nairobi as a sole proprietor. I'm thinking about registering my business formally and maybe applying for a government investment incentive in the future. Based on what you know about Kenya's business registration system, which government bodies should I be aware of, and what role do they play?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "For your retail shop, the key body to know about is the Business Registration Service (BRS), which is overseen by the Attorney General. The BRS manages the Companies Registry – this is where you'll register your business formally if you decide to move from sole proprietor to a registered company structure.\n\nIf later on you want to explore investment incentives or support to grow your business, Kenya Investment Authority (KenInvest) is the statutory body responsible for promoting investments in Kenya. They can advise on investment opportunities and incentives available to businesses like yours.\n\nRight now, focus on the BRS and Companies Registry for your registration needs. KenInvest becomes relevant once you're looking to scale or attract investment."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "doing_business_kenya_sectors.txt", "source_text": "attorney general Business Registration Service (BRS) is mandated to oversee the operations of the Companies Registry, Movable Property Security Rights Registry (Collateral Registry), Insolvency (Official Receivers) Registry and the Hire Purchase Registry php Kenya Investment Authority Kenya Investment Authority (KenInvest) is a statutory body established in 2004 through an Act of Parliament (Investment Promotion Act No 6 of 2004) with the main objective of promoting investments in Kenya It is r"}}
