{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I run a small fruit and vegetable stall in Mackinnon Market in Mombasa, and I'm renting space there. What fees do I need to pay according to the Mombasa County Finance Bill, 2024?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Based on the Mombasa County Finance Bill 2024, if you're renting a stall in Mackinnon Market for fruits and vegetables, your monthly rental fee is KSh 2,000.00. However, if your stall is in the front row of the market, the fee remains KSh 2,000.00 per month. Make sure you pay this fee on time each month to avoid non-compliance penalties. The County can charge you penalties for non-compliance with various fees, so keep your rental payments current to stay in good standing with the market authorities."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb1_legal_regulatory", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "mombasa_county_finance_act_2024.pdf", "source_text": "16 The Mombasa County Finance Bill, 2024 No. PARTICULARS AMOUNT Item of Charge KSh. 294 Non–Compliance of Encroachment fee 50,000.00 295 Non– Compliance of wall branding fee 100,000.00 E TRADE, TOURISM AND INVESTMENTS 30. MARKET STALLS/SHOP RENTALS Mackinnon Market 296 Stalls per month meats/chicken 1,700.00 297 Stalls per month fruits/vegetables 2,000.00 298 Stalls per month fruits/vegetables front row 2,000.00 299 Mini Shop 5,000.00 300 Small Shop 7,000.00 301 Large Shop 10,000.00 302 Cold ro"}}
