{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm a small manufacturing business in Nairobi and I need to hire trained workers. Can you give me a step-by-step guide on how to use ITAP to find and connect with training institutions for apprentices and trainees?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's how to work with ITAP to find trained workers:\n\n1. **Understand what ITAP is**: ITAP is a web portal that connects businesses like yours directly to training institutions across Kenya.\n\n2. **Register your business on ITAP**: Visit the portal and create an account for your manufacturing business to access available trainees.\n\n3. **Post your attachment/apprenticeship needs**: Clearly state the type of training you need (e.g. machine operation, welding, assembly) and how many trainees you can accommodate.\n\n4. **Browse available trainees**: Use ITAP to search for students from training institutions who match your business needs.\n\n5. **Connect with training institutions**: The portal links you directly to the institutions, so you can coordinate on trainees' availability and training schedules.\n\n6. **Reduce waiting time**: One benefit of using ITAP is that it cuts down the time it normally takes to find and place students in attachment positions.\n\n7. **Provide structured training**: Once trainees arrive, ensure they receive quality, practical training that meets industry standards.\n\nThis approach helps you find properly trained manpower while supporting Kenya's industrial training standards."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "tveta_journal_2024.pdf", "source_text": "National Agency in spearheading integrated industrial training at all levels in the industry. It is mission is to promote the highest standards in the quality and efficiency of industrial training in Kenya and ensure an adequate supply of properly trained manpower at all levels in the industry. ITAP is a web portal designed to link training institutions to the Industry. It is targeted at reducing the duration taken to attach students to attachment places, though the number of trainees seeking p"}}
