{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm thinking about enrolling in a technical vocational training course to improve my skills for my small business. How do I check if a training institute is properly registered and legitimate before I sign up and pay fees?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Here's a checklist to verify a training institute is legitimate before enrolling:\n\n1. **Check the TVETA Registration Number** — Ask the institute for their TVETA (Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority) registration code. It should be in the format TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/[number]/[year].\n\n2. **Verify the 'Registered and Licensed' Status** — Confirm the institute shows as 'Registered and Licensed' in official TVETA records. If they can't provide proof of this status, do not enroll.\n\n3. **Note the Registration Expiry Date** — Check when their registration expires. An institute with an expired license may not meet current standards.\n\n4. **Ask for Their Registration Details** — Legitimate institutes will openly share their TVETA registration details. If they refuse or seem unclear, that's a red flag.\n\n5. **Confirm the Institute Location** — Verify the physical address matches what's on their registration (e.g., Nairobi, Bungoma, Machakos).\n\n**Bottom line:** Never pay fees to an unregistered institute. Always request and verify their TVETA registration documents before committing your money."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "drafting", "source_filename": "tveta_accredited_institutions.txt", "source_text": "219/2025 TVC Private Bungoma 2030-11-05 Registered and Licensed Details 1659 Global Leadership Network Training Institute TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0220/2025 TVC Private Nairobi 2030-11-05 Registered and Licensed Details 1660 MAHANAIM EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTE TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0221/2016 TVC Private Nairobi 2026-07-13 Registered and Licensed Details 1661 Great Nairobi East College of Management and Technology TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0221/2025 TVC Private Machakos 2030-11-05 Registered and Licensed Details 1662 Ha"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm running a small vocational training centre in Nairobi with 15 trainees. We currently have classrooms, a basic computer lab, and a small office. According to Kenyan regulations, which facilities are we required to have that we might be missing?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Based on regulatory requirements for TVET institutions, you need to assess whether you have these essential facilities: a proper drainage system and sanitation facilities, a reliable water supply, health services (at least a basic health unit or arrangement with a clinic), and spaces for worship. You should also have outdoor recreation or sports facilities for your trainees. Since you mentioned having an ICT infrastructure (computer lab), that's good. The key gap to address immediately is ensuring proper sanitation, water, drainage, and health support—these are fundamental for any training institution. If your centre provides accommodation (residential), you'd additionally need kitchen and dining facilities plus trainee accommodation with laundry and storage. Even if non-residential now, plan for these as you grow. Make sure all facilities can accommodate your current 15 trainees and any projected growth."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "analysis", "source_filename": "tveta_accreditation_handbook.pdf", "source_text": "ies; h. Outdoor recreation facilities in form of games or sports facilities; i. Drainage system, proper sanitation and water supply; j. Health unit; k. ICT infrastructure; and l. Spaces of worship. In addition to the facilities provided above, a residential TVET institution shall provide: m. Kitchen and dining facilities; n. Trainee accommodation, including adequate laundry and storage facilities. NOTE: A TVET institution should have facilities that can accommodate the projected trainee populati"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm starting a small TVET training centre in Kenya and need to understand what basic facilities I must have in place. What does the law say are the essential facilities I need to provide?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "According to Kenya's TVET regulations, you need to provide these core facilities: outdoor recreation areas for games and sports, a proper drainage system with good sanitation and water supply, a health unit on site, ICT infrastructure, and spaces for worship. If your centre will have students staying overnight, you must also add kitchen and dining facilities, trainee accommodation with laundry and storage areas. The key point is that all these facilities need to be sized to handle the number of trainees you're planning to accommodate. Start by mapping out what you already have and what gaps need filling before you begin operations."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "summarization", "source_filename": "tveta_accreditation_handbook.pdf", "source_text": "ies; h. Outdoor recreation facilities in form of games or sports facilities; i. Drainage system, proper sanitation and water supply; j. Health unit; k. ICT infrastructure; and l. Spaces of worship. In addition to the facilities provided above, a residential TVET institution shall provide: m. Kitchen and dining facilities; n. Trainee accommodation, including adequate laundry and storage facilities. NOTE: A TVET institution should have facilities that can accommodate the projected trainee populati"}}
