{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant advising Kenyan MSME operators on tax, registration, financing, and regulatory compliance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "I'm thinking about enrolling in a vocational training course in Kenya. What does this document tell me about graduation rates and course options at vocational training centres?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Based on the source, vocational training centres in Kenya track graduation data by gender and course type. They offer both STEM courses (science, technology, engineering, maths-focused) and non-STEM courses like Secretarial Studies and Front Office Operations. The centres collect information on how trainees progress from one module or year to the next to measure graduation rates. This data is broken down by gender and separates private from public training centres, so you can see how different institutions perform. However, the specific graduation rate numbers aren't shown in this excerpt—you'd need to check the full table for those details when choosing your course."}], "_meta": {"kb_id": "kb7_culture_context", "task_type": "summarization", "source_filename": "tveta_annual_returns_report_2023.pdf", "source_text": "cluded Secretarial Studies and Front Office Operations. 5.3 Graduation Rate Graduation data collected from Vocational Training Centres was used to determine the trainee transitions from one module/ year of study to another. Table 26 provides the gender disaggregated graduation data in STEM and non-STEM courses for the private and public Vocational training Centres. Table 26 VTCs Graduation Data for 2023 Overa STEM Graduates Non-STEM Graduates ll Category Enrollme Male Femal Total Enrollme Male T"}}
